1
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:20,430
Cryogenic liquids are a specific type of compressed gas with their own set of hazards and precautions.

2
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:26,090
A cryogenic liquid is an extremely cold liquid that at normal temperature would be a gas.

3
00:00:26,090 --> 00:00:30,130
Due to their dependence on staying cold, cryogenic liquids may begin to boil violently

4
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:31,970
if stored at room temperature.

5
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:35,130
This puts cryogenic liquids in a category of their own when it comes to compressed

6
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:36,290
gases.

7
00:00:36,290 --> 00:00:39,570
With its special properties also come specific hazards.

8
00:00:39,570 --> 00:00:43,850
First, direct contact with cryogenic liquids can cause cold burns on the skin and even

9
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:45,150
frostbite.

10
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:49,070
Even touching the cylinders and piping containing these liquids can be dangerous as the coldness

11
00:00:49,070 --> 00:00:52,970
of the surface may cause the skin to stick to it, similar to the childhood dare of putting

12
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:55,190
your tongue on a cold metal pole.

13
00:00:55,190 --> 00:00:59,710
When cryogenic liquids are transferred to a warmer container, they can boil and splash,

14
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:01,750
increasing the risk for skin exposure.

15
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:06,470
Since they are a liquid, cryogens can condense and then re-freeze inside openings in the

16
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:07,470
cylinder.

17
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:11,150
When these openings are blocked, pressure can build up causing an explosion.

18
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:15,310
Cryogenic oxygen is extremely dangerous and can cause combustible substances to ignite

19
00:01:15,310 --> 00:01:17,910
and burn more easily or explode.

20
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:21,550
As with other compressed gases, there are certain steps that can be taken to use cryogenic

21
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:23,070
liquids safely.

22
00:01:23,070 --> 00:01:27,470
Since the ventilation of cryogenic liquids is important, using ventilation or oxygen

23
00:01:27,470 --> 00:01:29,830
sensors and alarms is recommended.

24
00:01:29,830 --> 00:01:33,310
These monitors should be checked frequently before and during use.

25
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:37,350
All equipment must be free of grease, oil, dirt, and other materials that are reactive

26
00:01:37,350 --> 00:01:40,590
when they come in contact with cryogens like liquid oxygen.

27
00:01:40,590 --> 00:01:45,190
Remember that cryogenic liquids can alter the make-up of materials, making them brittle,

28
00:01:45,190 --> 00:01:48,570
so you must choose the correct materials for the job.

29
00:01:48,570 --> 00:01:52,490
Cryogenic liquids should be stored in a special cylinder called a duer, which has a vacuum

30
00:01:52,490 --> 00:01:55,830
space between the liquid and the outer walls of the container.

31
00:01:55,830 --> 00:01:59,630
All duers must have pressure relief valves and loose fitting lids to prevent pressure

32
00:01:59,630 --> 00:02:00,630
build up.

33
00:02:00,630 --> 00:02:04,710
When cryogenic liquids need to be moved, at least two people should transport the

34
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:05,710
cylinder.

35
00:02:05,710 --> 00:02:09,190
Don't allow moisture to get inside the container as it may freeze, causing ice

36
00:02:09,190 --> 00:02:11,230
blocks in the relief valves.

37
00:02:11,230 --> 00:02:14,750
Finally, keep heat sources away from cryogenic liquids.

38
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:19,190
It's also important to protect yourself when handling cryogenic liquids.

39
00:02:19,190 --> 00:02:23,430
Appropriate personal protective equipment, or PPE, should be worn at all times.

40
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:26,990
This includes loose fitting gloves that can easily be thrown off as some liquid is spilled

41
00:02:26,990 --> 00:02:27,990
in them.

42
00:02:27,990 --> 00:02:31,390
The gloves should be leather or specific to cryogenic work.

43
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:36,390
Rubber gloves must never be used, as rubber hardens when exposed to cryogenic liquids.

44
00:02:36,390 --> 00:02:40,390
Sea shields and goggles will protect your eyes and face from accidental splashes.

45
00:02:40,390 --> 00:02:44,130
They need to fit tightly against the skin to prevent liquid from leaking in should a

46
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:45,710
splash occur.

47
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:49,890
Closed toed leather shoes are the best option when working with cryogenic liquids.

48
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:54,230
Leather naturally repels any spilled liquid, while absorbent materials like sneakers will

49
00:02:54,230 --> 00:02:56,150
draw the liquid toward your skin.

50
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:59,830
For this reason, a leather apron should also be worn over clothing.

51
00:02:59,830 --> 00:03:04,150
Metal jewelry like rings and watches shouldn't be worn when working with cryogenic liquid.

52
00:03:04,630 --> 00:03:08,910
If the skin does come in contact with a cryogenic liquid, run the effect into area under room

53
00:03:08,910 --> 00:03:11,610
temperature water for 15 minutes.

54
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:14,230
Never use very hot or very cold water.

55
00:03:14,230 --> 00:03:18,430
The rewarming of the skin should be done gradually and can take up to 60 minutes.

56
00:03:18,430 --> 00:03:22,310
If the area becomes frostbitten, seek medical attention immediately.

57
00:03:22,310 --> 00:03:26,910
The best way to prevent injury is to be familiar with using cryogenic liquids and to be careful.
